</h3></header><section>
<div class="os-note-body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1580825" class="unnumbered os-hasSolution"><header></header><section>
<div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1746360"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166492788998">Write each sentence as a proportion:

</p><ol id="eip-id1168469756973" type="1" class="circled"><li><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>6</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> is to <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>7</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> as <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>36</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> is to <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>

<li><span class="token">ⓑ</span> <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>8</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> adults for <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>36</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> children is the same as <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>12</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> adults for <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>54</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> children.</li>

<li><span class="token">ⓒ</span> <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>$3.75</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>$3.75</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math> for <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>6</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> ounces is equivalent to <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>$2.50</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>$2.50</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math> for <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>4</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> ounces.</li></ol></div></div>

</section></div>
</div></section></div>
<p id="fs-id1097912">Look at the proportions <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> and <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> From our work with equivalent fractions we know these equations are true. But how do we know if an equation is a proportion with equivalent fractions if it contains fractions with larger numbers?</p>
<p id="fs-id1166498443767">To determine if a proportion is true, we find the <strong>cross products</strong> of each proportion. To find the cross products, we multiply each denominator with the opposite numerator (diagonally across the equal sign). The results are called a cross product because of the cross formed. If, and only if, the given proportion is true, that is, the two sides are equal, then the cross products of a proportion will be equal.</p><span data-type="media" id="fs-id1731746" data-alt="The figure shows cross multiplication of two proportions. There is the proportion 1 is to 2 as 4 is to 8. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 8 · 1 = 8 and 2 · 4 = 8. There is the proportion 2 is to 3 as 6 is to 9. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 9 · 2 = 18 and 3 · 6 = 18.">
<button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The figure shows cross multiplication of two proportions. There is the proportion 1 is to 2 as 4 is to 8. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 8 · 1 = 8 and 2 · 4 = 8. There is the proportion 2 is to 3 as 6 is to 9. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 9 · 2 = 18 and 3 · 6 = 18." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/4d598a8f145db7190fa091790182407bdc3a3234" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The figure shows cross multiplication of two proportions. There is the proportion 1 is to 2 as 4 is to 8. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 8 · 1 = 8 and 2 · 4 = 8. There is the proportion 2 is to 3 as 6 is to 9. Arrows are shown diagonally across the equal sign to show cross products. The equations formed by cross multiplying are 9 · 2 = 18 and 3 · 6 = 18." width="390" height="62" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/4d598a8f145db7190fa091790182407bdc3a3234"></button>
</span>
<div data-type="note" id="fs-id1166489098476" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title" data-type="title">
  <span class="os-title-label" data-type="">Cross Products of a Proportion</span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="os-note-body">
<p id="fs-id1517408">For any proportion of the form <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> where <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> its cross products are equal.</p>
<span data-type="media" id="fs-id1166494770801" data-alt="The image demonstrates cross products of a proportion with numerator a multiplying with denominator d, and denominator b multiplying with numerator c.">
<button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image demonstrates cross products of a proportion with numerator a multiplying with denominator d, and denominator b multiplying with numerator c." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/b612159037d1b5e1ed3b580f1b5336b6ebb18b84" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image demonstrates cross products of a proportion with numerator a multiplying with denominator d, and denominator b multiplying with numerator c." width="87" height="71" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/b612159037d1b5e1ed3b580f1b5336b6ebb18b84"></button>
</span>
</div></section></div>
<p id="fs-id1501697">Cross products can be used to test whether a proportion is true. To test whether an equation makes a proportion, we find the cross products. If they are both equal, we have a proportion.</p>
<div data-type="example" id="fs-id1470247" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.41</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1166493760956" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1476424"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166497362535">Determine whether each equation is a proportion:

</p><ol id="eip-id1168466230295" type="1" class="circled"><li><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>28</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>28</mn></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>

<li><span class="token">ⓑ</span> <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>17.5</mn><mn>37.5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mn>17.5</mn><mn>37.5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li></ol></div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1946221" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
<p id="fs-id1491625">To determine if the equation is a proportion, we find the cross products. If they are equal, the equation is a proportion.</p>
<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1168468703669"><table data-id="eip-id1168468703669" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure shows the steps to finding the cross products of the proportion 4 is to 9 as 12 is to 28. The cross multiplication shown is 28 times 4 = 112 and 9 times 12 = 28." data-label="">
  <tbody>

 <tr>
   <td><span class="token">ⓐ</span> </td>
<td>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
   </td><td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467196647" data-alt="A mathematical equation showing the fractions 4/9 equals 12/28. Both fractions are written in black against a plain white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation showing the fractions 4/9 equals 12/28. Both fractions are written in black against a plain white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/d64818351ba2a0a0e92340041f796fefb99cb31b" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation showing the fractions 4/9 equals 12/28. Both fractions are written in black against a plain white background." width="226" height="40" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/d64818351ba2a0a0e92340041f796fefb99cb31b"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Find the cross products.</td>
 <td><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>112</mn><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mn>9</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>28</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>112</mn><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mn>9</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math><span data-type="newline"><br></span><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467113660" data-alt="The image illustrates an inequality between two fractions, 4/9 and 12/28, using cross-multiplication with blue arrows to show that 4 multiplied by 28 is not equal to 9 multiplied by 12."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image illustrates an inequality between two fractions, 4/9 and 12/28, using cross-multiplication with blue arrows to show that 4 multiplied by 28 is not equal to 9 multiplied by 12." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/d11d361bed9c691b2ff449dcf905e81a434dcbdf" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image illustrates an inequality between two fractions, 4/9 and 12/28, using cross-multiplication with blue arrows to show that 4 multiplied by 28 is not equal to 9 multiplied by 12." width="226" height="38" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/d11d361bed9c691b2ff449dcf905e81a434dcbdf"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

</tbody>
</table></div><p id="fs-id1166481190972">Since the cross products are not equal, <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> the equation is not a proportion.</p>


<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1168469699712"><table data-id="eip-id1168469699712" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure shows the steps to finding the cross products of the proportion 17.5 is to 37.5 as 7 is to 15. The cross multiplication shown is 15 times 17.5 = 262.5 and 37.5 times 7 = 262.5." data-label="">
  <tbody>

 <tr>
   <td><span class="token">ⓑ</span> </td>
<td>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
   </td><td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168469613430" data-alt="A mathematical equation displays the fraction 17.5/37.5 simplified to 7/15, demonstrating equivalence between the two ratios."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation displays the fraction 17.5/37.5 simplified to 7/15, demonstrating equivalence between the two ratios." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/222e3f66ed8139bf3bd781ccb826764f70e7ec94" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation displays the fraction 17.5/37.5 simplified to 7/15, demonstrating equivalence between the two ratios." width="292" height="42" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/222e3f66ed8139bf3bd781ccb826764f70e7ec94"></button>
</span></td>
 </tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Find the cross products.</td>
 <td><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>17.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>262.5</mn><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mn>37.5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>262.5</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>15</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>17.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>262.5</mn><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mn>37.5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>262.5</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math><span data-type="newline"><br></span>
<span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168466166406" data-alt="An equation showing 17.5 divided by 37.5 is equal to 7 divided by 15, with blue arrows illustrating the concept of cross-multiplication.">
<button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of An equation showing 17.5 divided by 37.5 is equal to 7 divided by 15, with blue arrows illustrating the concept of cross-multiplication." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/5c0f0c20acdf032e7eade463ca27bdbb3619cce1" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="An equation showing 17.5 divided by 37.5 is equal to 7 divided by 15, with blue arrows illustrating the concept of cross-multiplication." width="292" height="39" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/5c0f0c20acdf032e7eade463ca27bdbb3619cce1"></button>
</span></td>
 </tr>

</tbody>
</table></div><p id="fs-id1956342">Since the cross products are equal, <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>17.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>37.5</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>17.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>37.5</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> the equation is a proportion.</p>
</div>
</section>
      </details>
</section></div></div></section></div>
