<section data-depth="1" id="fs-id1166490756517"><h3 data-type="title">Solve Proportions</h3>
<p id="fs-id1166491085133">To solve a proportion containing a variable, we remember that the proportion is an equation. All of the techniques we have used so far to solve equations still apply. In the next example, we will solve a proportion by multiplying by the <span data-type="term" class="no-emphasis" id="term-00002" group-by="L">Least Common Denominator</span> (LCD) using the <span data-type="term" class="no-emphasis" id="term-00003" group-by="M">Multiplication Property of Equality</span>.</p>
<div data-type="example" id="fs-id1166492887204" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.42</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1685112" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1944367"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166494756631">Solve: <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1626522" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
