<div data-type="note" id="fs-id1362320" class="try ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Try It </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.90</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="os-note-body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1524849" class="unnumbered os-hasSolution"><header></header><section>
<div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1105678"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166498099744">For every <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>1</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> kilogram (kg) of a child’s weight, pediatricians prescribe <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>15</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> milligrams (mg) of a fever reducer. If Isabella weighs <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>12</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> kg, how many milligrams of the fever reducer will the pediatrician prescribe?</p>
</div></div>

