<div data-type="example" id="fs-id829816" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.46</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1438347" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1166495836173"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166498049903">One brand of microwave popcorn has <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>120</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>120</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> calories per serving. A whole bag of this popcorn has <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.5</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>3.5</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> servings. How many calories are in a whole bag of this microwave popcorn?</p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1518056" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1168466068741"><table data-id="eip-id1168466068741" class="unnumbered unstyled" data-summary="Outlines systematic steps to solve a word problem using proportions, illustrated by calculating total calories in a bag of microwave popcorn." data-label="" role="presentation">
  <tbody>

<tr>
<td>Identify what you are asked to find. </td>
<td>How many calories are in a whole bag of microwave popcorn?</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Choose a variable to represent it. </td>
<td>Let <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math> number of calories.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Write a sentence that gives the information to find it.</td>
<td>If there are 120 calories per serving, how many calories are in a whole bag with 3.5 servings?</td>
</tr>

 <tr>
   <td>Translate into a proportion.</td>
   <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467560815" data-alt="A mathematical equation shows that 'calories / serving' equals 'calories / serving,' representing an identity or a tautology in unit measurement."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation shows that 'calories / serving' equals 'calories / serving,' representing an identity or a tautology in unit measurement." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e9f9a3daaf9cdb44a79871f9de50c19d70b7fb8c" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation shows that 'calories / serving' equals 'calories / serving,' representing an identity or a tautology in unit measurement." width="185" height="45" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e9f9a3daaf9cdb44a79871f9de50c19d70b7fb8c"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Substitute given values.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467560833" data-alt="A mathematical equation shows a fraction 120 over 1 equal to the fraction c over 3.5. This represents a proportion where 120 divided by 1 is equal to c divided by 3.5."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation shows a fraction 120 over 1 equal to the fraction c over 3.5. This represents a proportion where 120 divided by 1 is equal to c divided by 3.5." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/83b01f09b06a0642ed21bf465c463cd785ab883e" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation shows a fraction 120 over 1 equal to the fraction c over 3.5. This represents a proportion where 120 divided by 1 is equal to c divided by 3.5." width="185" height="41" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/83b01f09b06a0642ed21bf465c463cd785ab883e"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

<tr>
 <td>Multiply both sides by 3.5.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468371113" data-alt="An algebraic equation: (3.5)(120/1) = (3.5)(c/3.5), demonstrating the multiplication of a decimal by a fraction on both sides."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of An algebraic equation: (3.5)(120/1) = (3.5)(c/3.5), demonstrating the multiplication of a decimal by a fraction on both sides." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/c1123569681b8a8358433b768e02941de65a77ba" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="An algebraic equation: (3.5)(120/1) = (3.5)(c/3.5), demonstrating the multiplication of a decimal by a fraction on both sides." width="185" height="42" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/c1123569681b8a8358433b768e02941de65a77ba"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Multiply.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467360492" data-alt="The image displays the mathematical equation '420 = c' in a simple, clear font against a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image displays the mathematical equation '420 = c' in a simple, clear font against a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/08790faed34113aa16bd39df2fb1f60eaf21ecf8" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image displays the mathematical equation '420 = c' in a simple, clear font against a white background." width="185" height="19" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/08790faed34113aa16bd39df2fb1f60eaf21ecf8"></button></span></td>
 </tr>
<tr>
<td> Check if the answer is reasonable. </td>
<td>
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td> Yes. Since 3.5 is between 3 and 4, the total calories should be between 360 (3⋅120) and 480 (4⋅120). </td>
<td>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td> Write a complete sentence. </td>
<td> The whole bag of microwave popcorn has 420 calories. </td>
</tr>

</tbody>
</table></div></div>
</section>
      </details>
</section></div></div></section></div>
<div data-type="note" id="fs-id1166492002952" class="try ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
