<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1166493708616" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1166492709163"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166490858582">Josiah went to Mexico for spring break and changed <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>$325</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>$325</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> dollars into Mexican pesos. At that time, the exchange rate had <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>$1</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>$1</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> U.S. is equal to <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>12.54</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>12.54</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> Mexican pesos. How many Mexican pesos did he get for his trip?</p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1166482704727" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1168469868734"><table data-id="eip-id1168469868734" class="unnumbered unstyled" data-summary="Step-by-step process for solving a currency conversion problem using proportions, detailing each stage from problem identification to final answer." data-label="" role="presentation">
  <tbody>

<tr>
<td>Identify what you are asked to find. </td>
<td>How many Mexican pesos did Josiah get?</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Choose a variable to represent it. </td>
<td>Let <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math> number of pesos.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Write a sentence that gives the information to find it.</td>
<td>If $1 U.S. is equal to 12.54 Mexican pesos, then $325 is how many pesos?</td>
</tr>

 <tr>
   <td>Translate into a proportion.</td>
   <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468387263" data-alt="A diagram showing the expression &quot;dollars per peso equals dollars per peso.&quot; The image illustrates that the ratio of dollars to pesos remains constant."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A diagram showing the expression &quot;dollars per peso equals dollars per peso.&quot; The image illustrates that the ratio of dollars to pesos remains constant." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/a1bf9db4cb9e9c5b65e2adc55de4a8a3a9f4e202" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A diagram showing the expression &quot;dollars per peso equals dollars per peso.&quot; The image illustrates that the ratio of dollars to pesos remains constant." width="164" height="45" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/a1bf9db4cb9e9c5b65e2adc55de4a8a3a9f4e202"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Substitute given values.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467114088" data-alt="A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background, showing 1 divided by 12.54 equals 325 divided by p."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background, showing 1 divided by 12.54 equals 325 divided by p." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/7436fd6c8c3d3f8a4aa1ef529ecbb31a7d8ff9f1" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background, showing 1 divided by 12.54 equals 325 divided by p." width="164" height="38" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/7436fd6c8c3d3f8a4aa1ef529ecbb31a7d8ff9f1"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

<tr>
 <td>The variable is in the denominator, so find the cross products and set them equal.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467352665" data-alt="The image displays the mathematical equation p * 1 = 12.54(325)."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image displays the mathematical equation p * 1 = 12.54(325)." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e815e9b85ada6fee6ea20bc86695d9f48a8a359e" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image displays the mathematical equation p * 1 = 12.54(325)." width="164" height="38" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e815e9b85ada6fee6ea20bc86695d9f48a8a359e"></button></span></td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
 <td>Simplify.</td>
 <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467352682" data-alt="A mathematical equation displays 'c = 4,075.5' in black font against a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation displays 'c = 4,075.5' in black font against a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ca55c8113af18f21a8e85cead34d12852cb308fe" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation displays 'c = 4,075.5' in black font against a white background." width="164" height="18" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ca55c8113af18f21a8e85cead34d12852cb308fe"></button></span></td>
 </tr>
<tr>
<td> Check if the answer is reasonable. </td>
<td>
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td> Yes, $100 would be $1,254 pesos. $325 is a little more than 3 times this amount.
</td>
<td>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td> Write a complete sentence. </td>
<td> Josiah has 4075.5 pesos for his spring break trip. </td>
</tr>


</tbody>
</table></div></div>
</section>
