<p id="fs-id1699747">Translate to a proportion. What number is <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>75%</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>75%</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>?</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1833179" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
<p id="fs-id1166492017953">If you look for the word "of", it may help you identify the base.<span data-type="newline"><br></span>

</p><div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1166828184051"><table data-id="eip-id1166828184051" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure shows the parts of a percent proportion in the question 'What number is 75% of 90?' It shows 'what number' as the amount, 75% as the percent, and 90 as the base." data-label="">
  <tbody>
  <tr>
    <td>Identify the parts of the percent proportion.</td>
    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1166821262634" data-alt="An image explaining parts of a percentage problem: 'What number is 75% of 90?'. 'What number' is the amount, '75%' is the percent, and '90' is the base. 'Of' is highlighted in red."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of An image explaining parts of a percentage problem: 'What number is 75% of 90?'. 'What number' is the amount, '75%' is the percent, and '90' is the base. 'Of' is highlighted in red." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/94714c48598f83e4c112c0bb948f2cf0835e4545" data-media-type="image/png" alt="An image explaining parts of a percentage problem: 'What number is 75% of 90?'. 'What number' is the amount, '75%' is the percent, and '90' is the base. 'Of' is highlighted in red." width="435" height="66" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/94714c48598f83e4c112c0bb948f2cf0835e4545"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Restate as a proportion.</td>

    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1166819463374" data-alt="A math problem asks: 'What number out of 90 is the same as 75 out of 100?' The number '90' is highlighted in red."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A math problem asks: 'What number out of 90 is the same as 75 out of 100?' The number '90' is highlighted in red." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/dfafd45cadc7da5e542037111c3c7b6e8941951e" data-media-type="image/png" alt="A math problem asks: 'What number out of 90 is the same as 75 out of 100?' The number '90' is highlighted in red." width="435" height="22" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/dfafd45cadc7da5e542037111c3c7b6e8941951e"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Set up the proportion. Let <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>number</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>number</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math>.</td>
    <td><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>75</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>75</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></td>
  </tr>
</tbody>
</table></div></div>
