<section data-depth="1" id="fs-id1432614"><h3 data-type="title">Translate and Solve Percent Proportions</h3>
<p id="fs-id1166484083924">Now that we have written percent equations as proportions, we are ready to solve the equations.</p>
<div data-type="example" id="fs-id1788998" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.51</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1166492076080" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1833323"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166490855869">Translate and solve using proportions: What number is <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>45%</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>45%</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>?</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>80</mn><mo>?</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1698394" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">


<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id4251535"><table data-id="eip-id4251535" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure shows the parts of a percent proportion in the question 'What number is 45% of 80?' It shows 'what number' as the amount, 45% as the percent, and 80 as the base." data-label="">
  <tbody>
  <tr>
    <td>Identify the parts of the percent proportion.</td>
    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1167304133055" data-alt="A math problem asks 'What number is 45% of 80?' with 'What number' labeled as amount, '45%' as percent, and '80' as base, illustrating how to identify parts of a percentage problem."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A math problem asks 'What number is 45% of 80?' with 'What number' labeled as amount, '45%' as percent, and '80' as base, illustrating how to identify parts of a percentage problem." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ef39da6c8844be2069591b2f555a6a3b5cec916a" data-media-type="image/png" alt="A math problem asks 'What number is 45% of 80?' with 'What number' labeled as amount, '45%' as percent, and '80' as base, illustrating how to identify parts of a percentage problem." width="436" height="67" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ef39da6c8844be2069591b2f555a6a3b5cec916a"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Restate as a proportion.</td>

    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id3247756" data-alt="A math problem asks: 'What number out of 80 is the same as 45 out of 100?'"><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A math problem asks: 'What number out of 80 is the same as 45 out of 100?'" class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/bd8b4054e474fbcaa870ab7a7ab797a379aa98ab" data-media-type="image/png" alt="A math problem asks: 'What number out of 80 is the same as 45 out of 100?'" width="436" height="26" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/bd8b4054e474fbcaa870ab7a7ab797a379aa98ab"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
<td>Set up the proportion. Let <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math> number. </td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168469774887" data-alt="A mathematical equation displays the fraction n over 80 set equal to the fraction 45 over 100, which is commonly used to represent a proportion or percentage problem."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation displays the fraction n over 80 set equal to the fraction 45 over 100, which is commonly used to represent a proportion or percentage problem." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/213f1f237690ae84bbde8a3e92b0709333b636dc" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation displays the fraction n over 80 set equal to the fraction 45 over 100, which is commonly used to represent a proportion or percentage problem." width="127" height="38" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/213f1f237690ae84bbde8a3e92b0709333b636dc"></button></span></td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Find the cross products and set them equal. </td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467168393" data-alt="A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 80 multiplied by 45'."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 80 multiplied by 45'." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ca32a5401a0df7b279202e173046625a884d0730" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 80 multiplied by 45'." width="127" height="21" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ca32a5401a0df7b279202e173046625a884d0730"></button></span></td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Simplify.</td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168464924388" data-alt="A mathematical equation is displayed, reading '100n = 3,600'. The numbers and variable 'n' are in a bold, dark font against a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation is displayed, reading '100n = 3,600'. The numbers and variable 'n' are in a bold, dark font against a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/1ecfd5cceb4e0eda10423289c3167396287525e4" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed, reading '100n = 3,600'. The numbers and variable 'n' are in a bold, dark font against a white background." width="127" height="18" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/1ecfd5cceb4e0eda10423289c3167396287525e4"></button></span></td>
</tr>

 <tr>
   <td>Divide both sides by 100.</td>
   <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168464924404" data-alt="A mathematical equation showing 100n divided by 100 equals 3,600 divided by 100. This step demonstrates dividing both sides of an equation by 100 to solve for 'n'."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation showing 100n divided by 100 equals 3,600 divided by 100. This step demonstrates dividing both sides of an equation by 100 to solve for 'n'." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/30e4f2921181a46f4ba2eaca3cf0329fa72948e4" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation showing 100n divided by 100 equals 3,600 divided by 100. This step demonstrates dividing both sides of an equation by 100 to solve for 'n'." width="127" height="39" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/30e4f2921181a46f4ba2eaca3cf0329fa72948e4"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

<tr>
<td>Simplify.</td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168464917165" data-alt="The image displays the equation n = 36 in bold, black mathematical text centered against a plain white background. The variable 'n' is followed by an equals sign and the number '36', indicating a simple numerical assignment."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image displays the equation n = 36 in bold, black mathematical text centered against a plain white background. The variable 'n' is followed by an equals sign and the number '36', indicating a simple numerical assignment." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/508f8505dcd2c2e17cc5a5971856fb55b9e76211" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image displays the equation n = 36 in bold, black mathematical text centered against a plain white background. The variable 'n' is followed by an equals sign and the number '36', indicating a simple numerical assignment." width="127" height="19" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/508f8505dcd2c2e17cc5a5971856fb55b9e76211"></button></span></td>
</tr>

<tr>
 <td>Check if the answer is reasonable. </td>
<td>
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td> Yes. 45 is a little less than half of 100 and 36 is a little less than half 80.</td>
<td>
</td></tr>

 <tr>
 <td>Write a complete sentence that answers the question.</td>
 <td>36 is 45% of 80.</td>
 </tr>

</tbody>
</table></div></div>
</section>
      </details>
</section></div></div></section></div>
