  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="os-note-body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1166493771343" class="unnumbered os-hasSolution"><header></header><section>
<div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1166479093244"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1361377">Translate and solve using proportions: What number is <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>85%</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>85%</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>?</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>40</mn><mo>?</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></div>

</section></div>
</div></section></div>
<p id="fs-id1465902">In the next example, the percent is more than <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> which is more than one whole. So the unknown number will be more than the base.</p>
<div data-type="example" id="fs-id1166483683514" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">6.52</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1166491410977" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1166484085537"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1166483694550">Translate and solve using proportions: <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mtext>125%</mtext></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtext>125%</mtext></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> of <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>25</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> is what number?</p>
</div></div>
<details data-type="solution" id="fs-id1166482688502" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
<div class="os-table os-unstyled-container" id="eip-id1165358285731"><table data-id="eip-id1165358285731" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure shows the parts of a percent proportion in the question '125% of 25 is what number?' It shows 125% as the percent, 25 as the base, and 'what number' as the amount." data-label="">
  <tbody>
  <tr>
    <td>Identify the parts of the percent proportion.</td>
    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1165367323904" data-alt="A math problem asking '125% is 25 of what number?', with '125%' labeled as 'percent', '25' as 'base', and 'what number?' as 'amount', demonstrating a percentage calculation."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A math problem asking '125% is 25 of what number?', with '125%' labeled as 'percent', '25' as 'base', and 'what number?' as 'amount', demonstrating a percentage calculation." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ab8849d752dac8c21660c6494404d9aedbc9d862" data-media-type="image/png" alt="A math problem asking '125% is 25 of what number?', with '125%' labeled as 'percent', '25' as 'base', and 'what number?' as 'amount', demonstrating a percentage calculation." width="437" height="63" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/ab8849d752dac8c21660c6494404d9aedbc9d862"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Restate as a proportion.</td>

    <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1165367094433" data-alt="A mathematical word problem asks: 'What number out of 25 is the same as 125 out of 100?'"><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical word problem asks: 'What number out of 25 is the same as 125 out of 100?'" class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/69805270fbba2e190e8d7c4b39d27b362b698af2" data-media-type="image/png" alt="A mathematical word problem asks: 'What number out of 25 is the same as 125 out of 100?'" width="437" height="23" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/69805270fbba2e190e8d7c4b39d27b362b698af2"></button></span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
<td>Set up the proportion. Let <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></annotation-xml></semantics></math> number. </td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468771195" data-alt="A mathematical equation showing the proportion n/25 = 125/100, where 'n' is an unknown variable. The equation is presented in a clear, digital format on a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation showing the proportion n/25 = 125/100, where 'n' is an unknown variable. The equation is presented in a clear, digital format on a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/21d8d603f674a0e6bad087a3a65f26e430cf570c" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation showing the proportion n/25 = 125/100, where 'n' is an unknown variable. The equation is presented in a clear, digital format on a white background." width="135" height="38" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/21d8d603f674a0e6bad087a3a65f26e430cf570c"></button></span></td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Find the cross products and set them equal. </td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468771212" data-alt="A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 25 multiplied by 125' in black text on a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 25 multiplied by 125' in black text on a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/51239052ba1ecac2921691496761245564a79883" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation shows '100 multiplied by n equals 25 multiplied by 125' in black text on a white background." width="135" height="21" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/51239052ba1ecac2921691496761245564a79883"></button></span></td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Simplify.</td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468464320" data-alt="The image displays the algebraic equation 100n = 3,125."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of The image displays the algebraic equation 100n = 3,125." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/0827e17a23cae6235e3d84c854eba8cdd474049e" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="The image displays the algebraic equation 100n = 3,125." width="135" height="18" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/0827e17a23cae6235e3d84c854eba8cdd474049e"></button></span></td>
</tr>

 <tr>
   <td>Divide both sides by 100.</td>
   <td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168468464336" data-alt="A mathematical equation shows '100n over 100 equals 3,125 over 100,' demonstrating how to solve for 'n' by dividing both sides by 100, which will result in n = 3,125."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical equation shows '100n over 100 equals 3,125 over 100,' demonstrating how to solve for 'n' by dividing both sides by 100, which will result in n = 3,125." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/079dfa031a0bdda73ccd1b3cf69222378d6ea984" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical equation shows '100n over 100 equals 3,125 over 100,' demonstrating how to solve for 'n' by dividing both sides by 100, which will result in n = 3,125." width="135" height="39" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/079dfa031a0bdda73ccd1b3cf69222378d6ea984"></button></span></td>
 </tr>

<tr>
<td>Simplify.</td>
<td><span data-type="media" id="eip-id1168467222146" data-alt="A mathematical expression 'n = 31.25' is displayed in a serif font on a white background."><button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A mathematical expression 'n = 31.25' is displayed in a serif font on a white background." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/0e66c280fcae312341e486f64cc2f939b30a7ed1" data-media-type="image/jpeg" alt="A mathematical expression 'n = 31.25' is displayed in a serif font on a white background." width="135" height="19" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/0e66c280fcae312341e486f64cc2f939b30a7ed1"></button></span></td>
</tr>


<tr>
 <td>Check if the answer is reasonable. </td>
<td>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td> Yes. 125 is more than 100 and 31.25 is more than 25.</td>
<td>
</td></tr>
 <tr>
 <td>Write a complete sentence that answers the question.</td>
 <td>125% of 25 is 31.25.</td>
 </tr>

</tbody>
</table></div></div>
</section>
      </details>
</section></div></div></section></div>
